# Service tokens for MCP servers + ops scripts — NAMES ONLY, never values (repo is public).
#
# Where the values live: gitignored .claude/settings.local.json, under "env". Claude Code loads
# that block into the environment of every session, then expands ${VAR} in .mcp.json and the
# tools/*.sh scripts read the same vars. No browser/OAuth login is needed for any of them.
# Guardrail: .claude/hooks/token-guard.sh asks the user before any use of SUPABASE_ADMIN_TOKEN,
# any read of settings.local.json, any env dump, and any write-shaped call to these APIs.
#
# RENDER_API_KEY — dashboard.render.com → Account Settings → API Keys. Account-wide.
#   render MCP: header `Authorization: Bearer ${RENDER_API_KEY}` (Render's OAuth rejects dynamic
#   client registration, so header auth is the only path). REST: tools/ops-get.sh render,
#   tools/render-env.sh. deploy-scope-guard pins commands to the prod + staging service ids
#   (listed in its header).
RENDER_API_KEY=
#
# VERCEL_TOKEN — vercel.com/account/settings/tokens. Scoped to the `rasifiters` project only.
#   The Vercel MCP does NOT accept it (OAuth-only — 503 "token validation" on every attempt), and
#   the Vercel CLI refuses it (it must load the user, 404 for a project token). Use REST:
#   tools/ops-get.sh vercel '<path>' (deployments, build events, project, env metadata).
#   Not reachable with it: historical request logs (Hobby keeps ~1 h anyway).
VERCEL_TOKEN=
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN — supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens → Project scope `rasifiters`,
#   READ-ONLY preset. The default for every read, no prompts. supabase-rasifiters MCP sends it as
#   `Authorization: Bearer ${SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN}` (with read_only=true in the URL); REST:
#   tools/ops-get.sh supabase, tools/supabase-logs.sh (auth/edge/postgres logs).
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#
# SUPABASE_ADMIN_TOKEN — same page, Project scope `rasifiters`, FULL ACCESS. Deliberate changes
#   only (auth settings, staging infra). Every command that names it prompts the user
#   (token-guard). Never wired into an MCP server. Data/schema changes still go only through
#   user-run migrations in apps/backend/sql/.
SUPABASE_ADMIN_TOKEN=
